    "summary": "Deleted src/mcp/sampling-bridge.ts, src/agent/providers/mcp-sampling-provider.ts, runWithSamplerContext and currentSamplerContext (with the sampler AsyncLocalStorage), and both sampler branches of buildShaperProvider (explicit overrides.sampler and the ambient context; ShaperProviderOverrides loses sampler and modelHints, which nothing else used), with their tests: sampling-bridge.test.ts, mcp-sampling-provider.test.ts, sampler-context.test.ts and the five sampler cases of shaper-provider.test.ts. The remaining shaper-provider cases are unchanged and pass. Stale comments describing the in-process MCP/sampling design were updated (server.ts header, analyze-oneshot.ts, role-router.ts); tool descriptions are untouched (the t9 surface test pins them). New src/mcp/__tests__/sampling-retired.test.ts scans every non-test .ts under src for the bridge, the provider and the sampler-context names and checks both files are gone; a re-added mention fails it. DEVIATION from the task text, stated openly: progress-forward.ts and its test are KEPT. The plan called it unused, but since t9 the forwarders relay step.call progress through its mcpProgressSink (src/mcp/server.ts), so deleting it would remove code in use; neither acceptance check concerns it. model-failure.test.ts keeps two example error strings with the old provider's name as classifier input data. Full sweep in docs/epics/complete-consistent-richer-code-index-one-E20261011c2ba6fa6/S011/sweeps.md: nothing newly failing (MCPSection timing flake, 3 of 3 alone).",
